{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1062","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1062","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1062\",\"parent_revision\":\"9535f1c4f5ae0ee9c0094128f11daeb475cf51f6\",\"root_revision\":\"8bab570da3389a59360e873ff3e81feff0d8338e855fc709d18521d4dd4f92d8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Runaway sessions in wave dispatch are a real cost risk. Budget caps exist but turns-based loop detection is a separate circuit breaker. High-value protection for long milestone runs.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Wave items that loop indefinitely block the entire wave from completing, stalling the milestone.\\n- Bottleneck: Without a turns cap, a single stuck session holds its semaphore slot in `dispatch_spawn`, throttling concurrency for the entire wave.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Prevents infinite agentic loops in CI/CD-style wave dispatch with a complementary circuit breaker to `--max-budget-usd`.\\n- Operators can tune aggressiveness per wave item (simple grooming vs. complex implementation) once the field exists in the dispatch plan schema.\\n- Completes the dual-cap safety pattern documented in research (`--max-turns` + `--max-budget-usd`) for all spawned sessions.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `--max-turns N` is passed to `spawn.py spawn`, the spawned `claude` session exits after N turns. The `work-milestone` dispatch includes a configurable turns cap in its spawn command. A session that hits the cap exits with a non-zero code; `dispatch_spawn` treats it as a failed item and marks it accordingly in dispatch state.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nAfter this work is done:\\n- `spawn.py spawn --help` includes a `--max-turns INT` flag.\\n- `_build_spawn_shell_cmd` in `spawn.py` conditionally appends `--max-turns N` to the claude argv when the flag is supplied.\\n- `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool in `server.py` accepts an optional `max_turns` parameter (alongside the existing `model` parameter) and threads it through `_build_spawn_cmd` and `_run_spawn_item`.\\n- `_build_spawn_cmd` in `server.py` conditionally appends `--max-turns` to the spawn.py invocation.\\n- `work-milestone/SKILL.md` spawn command template includes `--max-turns {N}` with a documented sensible default.\\n- The dispatch plan schema documents an optional `max_turns` field per wave item and a plan-level default.\\n\\n**Architecture note**: `spawn.py` uses interactive tmux mode (`--worktree --tmux --dangerously-skip-permissions`), NOT `-p` mode. The `--max-turns` CLI flag documented in the research is for `-p` (print/headless) mode. Before implementing, verify that `--max-turns` is honored in interactive REPL mode; if not, the mechanism for turn-capping interactive sessions needs to be identified (e.g., a wrapper that counts turns and sends Ctrl-C, or switching to `-p` mode for dispatch).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py spawn --help` output contains `--max-turns`.\\n2. `uv run plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py spawn --max-turns 50 'test prompt'` spawns a session; inspecting the tmux launch command or claude argv confirms `--max-turns 50` was passed to claude.\\n3. `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool schema (via `uv run plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py --help` or MCP introspection) shows `max_turns` as an optional integer parameter.\\n4. `work-milestone/SKILL.md` spawn command template text includes `--max-turns` with a visible default value (e.g., 200).\\n5. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py` exits 0 (no lint regressions).\\n6. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` exits 0.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /kage-bunshin |\\n| Skill | /work-milestone |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py \u2014 `_build_spawn_shell_cmd` (line 476), argparse `--max-budget` (line 1017) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py \u2014 `_build_spawn_cmd` (line 2727), `_run_spawn_item` (line 2808), `dispatch_spawn` (line 2889) |\\n| Prior work | research/developer-tools/claude-code-cli-power-patterns.md \u2014 Tip 10: Headless CI/CD with Hard Budget Caps |\\n| Related item | #1061 \u2014 Add --effort flag (same files, same pattern, parallel item) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (standalone; can be implemented in parallel with #1061)\\n- Blocks: None directly; once done, wave dispatch is safer for long milestone runs\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall-Medium \u2014 Adding the argparse flag and threading it through `_build_spawn_shell_cmd`, `_build_spawn_cmd`, and `dispatch_spawn` is mechanical (< 40 lines of Python across 2 files). The uncertainty is the architecture note: if `--max-turns` does not apply to interactive mode, effort grows significantly. Resolving the architecture question is a prerequisite.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- **Architecture gap**: `spawn.py` uses interactive tmux mode, not `-p` mode. The `--max-turns` flag documented in the research (Tip 10) targets `-p` headless mode. Whether it is honored in interactive REPL sessions must be verified before implementing \u2014 this could change the entire implementation approach.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Does `--max-turns` apply to interactive REPL mode (`--worktree --tmux`) or only to `-p` (print) mode? If interactive mode ignores it, what is the intended capping mechanism for spawned kage-bunshin sessions?\\n- What is the preferred default cap for wave work sessions (e.g., 200 turns for a full work-backlog-item flow)?\\n- Should `max_turns` be configurable per wave item in the dispatch plan YAML, or is a single plan-level default sufficient?\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `spawn.py spawn --help` shows `--max-turns` flag.\\n2. `work-milestone/SKILL.md` spawn command template includes `--max-turns` and `--max-budget-usd`.\\n3. A spawned session with `--max-turns 50` exits after 50 turns even if work remains.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add --max-turns safety cap to kage-bunshin spawn and work-milestone dispatch** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`spawn.py` accepts `--max-turns` flag and passes it through to the `claude` CLI invocation. `work-milestone/SKILL.md` spawn command template includes both `--max-turns {N}` and `--max-budget-usd {N}` with configurable defaults. The dispatch plan schema includes optional `max_turns` and `max_budget` fields per wave item, with plan-level defaults.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`work-milestone/SKILL.md` spawns `claude -p` sessions per wave item with `--model sonnet --permission-mode auto --output-format json` but passes neither `--max-turns` nor `--max-budget-usd`. The kage-bunshin skill supports `--max-budget` but not `--max-turns`. A runaway agent in a wave item can loop indefinitely, consuming API credits and blocking the wave from completing. Budget caps alone have gaps -- a session can burn through turns doing no useful work while staying under budget.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/claude-code-cli-power-patterns.md -- pattern: Headless CI/CD with Hard Budget Caps\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4189990be181332d47e0dee3960e1cc00cf861aac81d7c138520cf6711499856\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS_FsA\"}"}